WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.787
On this slide, we are focusing on index and slice a list.

00:00:03.787 --> 00:00:08.452
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.452 --> 00:00:16.617
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:16.617 --> 00:00:18.997
Indexing retrieves one position, while slicing retrieves a range.

00:00:18.997 --> 00:00:24.397
Python indexing starts at zero and slice endpoints are usually exclusive.

00:00:24.397 --> 00:00:27.602
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:27.602 --> 00:00:33.752
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:33.752 --> 00:00:37.092
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:42.106
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
